                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e185ba72-215f-415e-b07c-f3252990ea69",
                                                "sense_id": "ee521b48-6ee3-3c37-b23c-840553650c10",
                                                "text": "For he [Alexander the Great] was not (as his father Philip [II of Macedon]) deſirous of all kind of glorie: who like a Rhetoritian had a delight to vtter his eloquence, and ſtamped in his coines, the victories he had wonne at the Olympian games, by the ſwift running of his horſe and coaches. For when he was asked one day (becauſe he was ſwift of foot) whether he would aſſay to run for victorie at the Olympian games: I could be content, ſaid he, ſo I might run with kings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "906d8783-88fd-4cdb-971a-e4f3c419fb54",
                                                "sense_id": "ee521b48-6ee3-3c37-b23c-840553650c10",
                                                "text": "The Olympian Games were celebrated at the Full Moon after the Somer Solſtice, ſo the Olympian Years begin at that Seaſon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f6c4162-c9ed-4d82-91dc-b042d40c29c4",
                                                "sense_id": "ee521b48-6ee3-3c37-b23c-840553650c10",
                                                "text": "During his Exile he [Cimon Coalemos] obtain'd the Olympian Prize in the Quadrijugal Chariot-race, and transferr'd the Honour to Miltiades [the Elder] his Mother's Son."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c80ed24d-a32d-461c-9093-c4f7801ef59b",
                                                "sense_id": "ee521b48-6ee3-3c37-b23c-840553650c10",
                                                "text": "Q. Were Women allow'd to be preſent at thoſe Games? / A. At firſt they were ſo ſtrict in this reſpect, that any Women who croſs'd the River Alpheus while theſe Games were celebrating, were condemn'd to be tumbled down a Rock. But afterwards, Women were even ſuffer'd to perform in the Olympian Games, and they ſometimes won the Prizes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed9aff10-e636-3fc8-a4a6-8fe148616eff",
                                        "entry_id": "1d765907-fff2-3d10-94c8-a3a77cbb29c0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to the modern Olympic Games; Olympic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Olympian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3753b960-5577-368a-aa63-1f0778d7bdf8",
                                        "entry_id": "63716df2-f40e-3832-9ade-caa25da02d43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An inhabitant of the city of Olympia, the capital of Washington, United States."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c41d98a-a36f-37b0-950f-95efdf55637c",
                                        "entry_id": "63716df2-f40e-3832-9ade-caa25da02d43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sportsperson competing in the ancient Olympic Games."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5944d241-2f65-4574-907d-8b754a27f2ee",
                                                "sense_id": "8c41d98a-a36f-37b0-950f-95efdf55637c",
                                                "text": "And I haue ſeene thee pauſe, and take thy breath, / When that a ring of Greekes haue ſhruped thee in, / Like an Olympian wraſtling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f42dd5c2-c023-3b2c-8e0c-35156371f146",
                                        "entry_id": "63716df2-f40e-3832-9ade-caa25da02d43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sportsperson competing in the modern Olympic Games."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8197708e-c1cf-4c73-83c4-a55d746e4fe9",
                                                "sense_id": "f42dd5c2-c023-3b2c-8e0c-35156371f146",
                                                "text": "I will forever carry the pride and privilege of representing this amazing country on the grandest global stage. There is so much that comes with that, with being an Olympian. But now, because of Covid-19, some athletes will never get that honour. […] There will be people who were getting the timing right for 2020 who won't be in 2021. From in one year does not guarantee form in the next. That is absolutely heart-breaking. There will be athletes in the community that should have become Olympians. Because of Covid-19, they will never get that opportunity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe8adf5a-d3a6-4592-b111-84cd04ef339d",
                                                "sense_id": "f42dd5c2-c023-3b2c-8e0c-35156371f146",
                                                "text": "[…] Olympians’ mental health has never been a key concern for the sports governing bodies that oversee them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
